Project Demonstration Phase
The Project Demonstration Phase is the stage where the completed project or prototype is presented to others. The main goal is to show how the project works and explain its features and benefits.
Key steps:
Introduce the project – Explain the project and its purpose.
Show the working model – Demonstrate the main features.
Explain the process – Describe how the project works.
Present the results – Show the output or benefits achieved.
Answer questions – Clear doubts and receive feedback.
Collect feedback – Use suggestions to improve the project.
